[{:db/id 17592186161754 :question/problem "![](images/5c/5c5e52c78f925dc4e01b1098b507865407f9848cc1db6e8a946ad81840e8e4ee.png)\n\n  \n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X \\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nI. $f(2) = 4$\n\nII. $\\exists\\, y \\in Y$ such that $\\forall\\, x \\in X,$ we have $f(x) \\neq y$\n\nIII. The function $f:X \\to Y$ is **into**" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161921 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ba992cb2-fd2f-5e4c-b95b-b82e7bb29b58"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161755 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ which is given by $f(x)=(x-1)^2-2?$\n\nI. The range of $f$ is $[-2, \\infty)$\n\nII. $\\forall\\, y \\in [-2, \\infty),$ $\\exists\\, x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\nIII. $f$ maps $\\mathbb{R}$ **into** $\\mathbb{R}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186161756 :question/problem "Which of the following functions are **into** functions?\n\nI. $f: [-2, \\infty) \\to \\mathbb{R}$ defined by $f(x) =\\sqrt{ x+2}$\n\nII. $g: \\mathbb{R} \\to [0, \\infty)$ defined by $g(x) = |x-2|+3$\n\nIII. $h:(0,\\infty) \\to\\Bbb R$ defined by $h(x) = \\ln(x)$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410015 :question/problem "![](images/ae/ae980a05fc0d25d2696185c88fcf90ff156af9c3f42af7cece80f8c33692a3d7.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nI. $f(1)=7$\n\nII. $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y$\n\nIII. The function $f:X\\to Y$ is **into**" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162235 :question/problem "![](images/b3/b3c5df109b00450c20acdbc07378bfe309cf808c1244bedd6ff4fa3a850ccd13.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nI. $f(10)=25$\n\nII. $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y$\n\nIII. The function $f:X\\to Y$ is not **into**" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410007 :question/problem "![](images/37/373448202bfd022f5629219b2c176f4096e4eeae275c1095798d77be92122cc2.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nI. $f(1)=4$\n\nII. $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y$\n\nIII. The function $f:X\\to Y$ is **into**" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410013 :question/problem "![](images/7f/7f68e70397b982a70b372b2bd9e4f73da3374d3abfb2ef4bbd2ec1fffe6dbb31.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:X\\to Y$ represented by the mapping diagram above?\n\nI. $f(2)=4$\n\nII. $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y$\n\nIII. The function $f:X\\to Y$ is **into**" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410011 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)?$\n\nI. The range of $f$ is $(0,\\infty )$\n\nII. $∀\\,y\\in R$ $∃\\,x\\in (0,\\infty )$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\nIII. $f$ maps $(0,\\infty )$ **into** $R$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410006 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)=2-{x}^{2}?$\n\nI. The range of $f$ is $(-\\infty ,-2]$\n\nII. $∀\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,2],$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\nIII. $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162568 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={3}^{x}?$\n\nI. The range of $f$ is $(0,\\infty )$\n\nII. $∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\nIII. $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ba992cb2-fd2f-5e4c-b95b-b82e7bb29b58" :question/id #uuid "ba992cb2-fd2f-5e4c-b95b-b82e7bb29b58" :question/math-academy-id "q-232536" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={3}^{x}+1?$\n\nI. The range of $f$ is $(1,\\infty )$\n\nII. $∀\\,y\\in (1,\\infty ),$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\nIII. $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$" :question/worked-solution "First, we graph the function.\n\n![](images/0c/0cb3e23cecdbd82803f5757827f21a424672bdde6da03782ca995d23e1c4d7b4.png)\n\nRecall that $f:X\\to Y$ is an *into* function if it is not a surjection. In other words, there exists an element $y$ in $Y$ such that it has no preimage in $X:$ \n\n$f:X\\to Y$ is an into function if $∃\\,y\\in Y$ such that $∀\\,x\\in X,$ we have $f(x)\\ne y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph, the function takes all $y$-values greater than $y=1$, excluding $y=1$ itself. So the range of the function is indeed $(1,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since the range of the function is $(1,\\infty )$, then for all $y$ contained within $(1,\\infty ),$ there exists some $x$ contained within $R$ such that $f(x)=y.$\n\n- Statement III is true. As we can see from the range, there is no real number $x$ such that $f(x)=0\\in R.$ So, $f$ maps $R$ *into* $R.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ed30b9dd-3daf-5001-88c4-b9152d2bad1b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed30b9dd-3daf-5001-88c4-b9152d2bad1b" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed30b9dd-3daf-5001-88c4-b9152d2bad1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fda4827e-23cb-5c38-a966-819a735816cd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fdee9ac7-df88-5be7-8e6b-0c2c8b6fd156" "answer-1b642c0e-8b84-5e4a-891d-2e1beb9ad37e" "answer-fda4827e-23cb-5c38-a966-819a735816cd" "answer-593420ae-cc21-52d8-a8ed-d92dcd3ab3f2" "answer-b08a5b5d-77ac-5e98-91fc-de49ca37b422"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdee9ac7-df88-5be7-8e6b-0c2c8b6fd156" :answer/id #uuid "fdee9ac7-df88-5be7-8e6b-0c2c8b6fd156" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b642c0e-8b84-5e4a-891d-2e1beb9ad37e" :answer/id #uuid "1b642c0e-8b84-5e4a-891d-2e1beb9ad37e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fda4827e-23cb-5c38-a966-819a735816cd" :answer/id #uuid "fda4827e-23cb-5c38-a966-819a735816cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-593420ae-cc21-52d8-a8ed-d92dcd3ab3f2" :answer/id #uuid "593420ae-cc21-52d8-a8ed-d92dcd3ab3f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b08a5b5d-77ac-5e98-91fc-de49ca37b422" :answer/id #uuid "b08a5b5d-77ac-5e98-91fc-de49ca37b422" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410009 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to R$ which is given by $f(x)={2}^{-x}?$\n\nI. The range of $f$ is $[0,\\infty )$\n\nII. $∀\\,y\\in R,$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\nIII. $f$ maps $R$ **into** $R$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162567 :question/problem "Which of the following functions are **into** functions?\n\nI. $f:R\\to (0,\\infty )$ defined by $f(x)={2}^{x}$\n\nII. $g:Q\\to Q$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{4}$\n\nIII. $h:R\\to R$ defined by $h(x)={5}^{x}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410010 :question/problem "Which of the following functions are **into** functions?\n\nI. $f:[0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=\\sqrt{x}$\n\nII. $g:R\\to [0,\\infty )$ defined by $g(x)={x}^{2}$\n\nIII. $h:R\\to [0,\\infty )$ defined by $h(x)={e}^{x}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410008 :question/problem "Which of the following functions are **into** functions?\n\nI. $f:R\\to R$ defined by $f(x)={x}^{3}$\n\nII. $g:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)$\n\nIII. $h:R\\to [0,\\infty )$ defined by $h(x)={e}^{x}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410012 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $f:R\\to (-\\infty ,1)$ which is given by $f(x)=1-{2}^{x}?$\n\nI. The range of $f$ is $(-\\infty ,1)$\n\nII. $∀\\,y\\in (-\\infty ,1],$ $∃\\,x\\in R$ such that $f(x)=y$\n\nIII. $f$ is a function of $R$ **into** $(-\\infty ,1)$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186410014 :question/problem "Which of the following functions are **into** functions?\n\nI. $f:(0,\\infty )\\to R$ defined by $f(x)=-{log}_{2}⁡(x)$\n\nII. $h:R\\to (0,\\infty )$ defined by $h(x)={3}^{x}$\n\nIII. $g:Q\\to R$ defined by $g(x)=\\sqrt[3]{x}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
